# Build an Elf Rogue 7 / Assassin 3 and photograph his Sneak Attack dice.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. bd inc-0rw, the parity half of the stacking defect. The
# Assassin's prose (lib/prestige.irh:547) adds his assassin levels to his
# rogue levels for Sneak Attack. Both grants read
#   Ability[CA_SNEAK_ATTACK,+1] at every 2nd level starting at 1st
# (lib/classes.irh:2561 and lib/prestige.irh:590), and each one counts only
# its own class. Seven rogue levels round up to four dice and three assassin
# levels round up to two, so the pre-fix character holds six. Ten levels at
# one die per two levels, with the first level's die given once, is five and
# a half, which floors to five. The rounding was happening twice.
#
# THE ORACLE is the sheet's Specials block, which prints the dice as
# "Sneak Attack +Nd6" from AbilityLevel(CA_SNEAK_ATTACK).
#
# WHY SEVEN AND THREE. Both numbers are odd, which is the only shape that
# shows the defect: an odd level count is where a class rounds its own half
# die up to a whole one. Rogue 5 / Assassin 2 -- the control this suite
# already runs -- is odd plus even, and its arithmetic is the same either way.
#
# SEED. The attribute rolls and the offered feats vary with the seed, so the
# feat picks stay positional and a seed is passed.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Rogue"
a                       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
@choose "Neutral"       # the class refuses a Good alignment
@choose "Alertness"
@until "Unspent Skill Ranks" a          # however many feats are asked for

# Eighteen ranks, two to a skill. The four the Assassin's gate reads first;
# the rest only because character generation will not release a character
# with a rank unspent.
@cursorto:mark "Disguise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Poison Use" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Bluff" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Alchemy" UP
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Appraise" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Balance" DOWN
RIGHT*3
@cursorto:mark "Climb" DOWN
RIGHT*3
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d                               # character sheet
@until "Class  Rogue 7" G       # seven core levels
@dump:rogue7

# The gate wants Disguise 10, Poison Use 10, Hide 7 and Move Silently 7.
# ISkillLevel (src/Create.cpp:3955) counts training and the inherent
# attribute bonus as well as ranks, so filling each to its cap clears them.
S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Disguise" DOWN
RIGHT*10
@cursorto:mark "Poison Use" DOWN
RIGHT*10
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" UP
RIGHT*10
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" UP
RIGHT*10
ENTER y

P                               # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Assassin"
@expect "Assassin 0"            # the gate let him in

# TWO THINGS MAKE THIS LOOP LOOK ODD, and both are the game, not the script.
#
# 1. The sheet does not redraw itself once a prestige class is on it. A level
#    gained while it is on screen leaves the old class line in place, so every
#    level below leaves the sheet and re-opens it, and the class line is read
#    only from a fresh one.
# 2. The Assassin's 1st level hands over a spellbook
#    (lib/prestige.irh:609-619). The item lands in the In-the-Air slot, and
#    the game will not leave inventory mode while anything is there -- so it
#    must be stowed before any further keystroke is spent, or every key after
#    it goes into the inventory screen instead. That is the lone 's' below.
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Assassin"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC                             # leave the sheet
s                               # stow the spellbook
ESC                             # leave the inventory
d                               # sheet again, freshly drawn
@expect "Assassin 1"

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Assassin"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
d
@expect "Assassin 2"

@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Assassin"
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
ESC
d
@expect "Assassin 3"
@dump:assassin3

W                       # Write Dump
a s s n 7 ENTER         # filename: "assn7"
ESC
@quit
